  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="poria-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">פוריא</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">pwryʾ</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">poriaʾ</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa">פוריה</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">pwryh</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">poriyah</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="poria-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>summer-fruits</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ὀπώρα</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אמר ר' לוי לא יגרע מצדיק עינו דיגמה 
                     <app>
                        <lem>דידיה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V">דידיה כאיניש דאמ' עינוהי דפוריה</rdg>
                     </app> תפסה לאה פלך הודייה ועמדו כל בניה בעלי הודיה</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">71,5</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 828: [Notes]</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">דיגמה</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Lewi said: He withdraweth not His eyes from the righteous (Hi 36, 7), meaning, his like, as the folk say: “fruit of its type”. Leah made hodiyah her métier, and so all her descendants did likewise.</quote>
                  </cit>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Only in K and V. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy IV 17b</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Jastrow II 1146ab</bibl>. Not to be confused with <term xml:lang="jpa">פוריא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">pwryʾ</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">φορεῖον</term> (cf. Krauss ibid.); not in GenR. Other spellings: <term xml:lang="jpa">פורין</term>. Cf. <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אפורייא</ref></note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Κrauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>433b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
